<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Offers fall as exports slow.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Offers fall as exports slow.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rail soybean meal offers slipped on Friday on persistent ideas export demand was tapering off, cash brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;There's a little bit of meal available,&quot; a Tennesee broker said. &quot;Export has slowed down a little bit.&quot;</p>
<p>Movement was very slow following Thursday's Thanksgiving Day holiday. Several basis offers were unavailable as offices were closed on Friday.</p>
<p>Domestic demand continued strong as cold weather gripped much of the country. But forecasts for warmer temperatures next week slowed buying interest.  </p>
